<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Lukka</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 BCE – 1180 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Lukka, a land of independent communities in south-western Anatolia, known as raiders and seafarers in Hittite and Egyptian texts.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Lukka lands lay in the coastal mountains of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, in later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lycian-dynasts">Lycia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisidia">Pisidia</a>. Hittite records from the 15th century BCE show them as Luwian-speaking communities without a single king, outside or at the edge of Hittite authority.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Lukka people served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> as troops, fighting at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kadesh">Kadesh</a>, and raided neighbours by sea; an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhetaten">Amarna</a> letter from the king of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-alashiya">Alashiya</a> complains of their yearly attacks. They had no central government, which made them hard to control.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Lukka appear among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-peoples">Sea Peoples</a> who attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merneptah">Merneptah</a> in the late 13th century BCE. After the Hittite collapse their land became the heartland of the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lycians">Lycians</a>, whose name continues theirs.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lukka.jpg" alt="Lukka" width="320" height="197"><figcaption>Image: Al-qamar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hethiter.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 BCE – 1180 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Luwian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luwian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Lukka Lands</dd></dl></aside></div>

